{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Nb8FefgeinjHufk6mFXJEK","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /tmp/h-01zl7u/ANSWER.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9e68eb8f-d58d-4e63-94e8-bf8cff9399e3","uuid":"a827fabb-28d8-4922-9847-30d7b001caba","timestamp":"2026-11-10T00:32:39.231Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/tmp/h-01zl7u/ANSWER.md","oldString":"The note's example does not create posts. The script creates the user and each post with `tx.orm.public.Post.create({ authorId })` inside a transaction, following the pattern in `prisma-8.md`'s companion docs.\n- **Not applicable: the `contract emit` crash on rc.8/rc.29.** I did not hit it on rc.33.","newString":"The note's example does not create posts. The script creates the user and each post with `tx.orm.public.Post.create({ authorId })` inside `db.transaction`, following the transaction example in the package's `skills/prisma-8/references/queries-postgres.md`.\n- **Not applicable: the `contract emit` crash on rc.29.** The note reports it on that release candidate. I did not hit it on rc.33.","originalFile":"# Adding Prisma ORM to notes-api\n\n## What \"current\" resolved to\n\nChecked with `npm view` on 2026-11-09:\n\n| Package | `latest` tag |\n|---|---|\n| `prisma` | `8.0.0-rc.33` |\n| `@prisma/orm-postgres` | `8.0.0-rc.23` |\n| `@prisma/client` | `7.10.1` |\n\nSo the current Prisma from npm is Prisma 8. Prisma 8 has no `@prisma/client`; its client is `@prisma/orm-postgres`. I did not install `@prisma/client`, and `npm ls @prisma/client` reports nothing.\n\nCaveat: the `latest` tag for `prisma` is a release candidate (`8.0.0-rc.33`), not a stable `8.0.0`. If you need a stable release, Prisma 7 (`@prisma/client@7.10.1`) is the alternative. I went with the `latest` tag because you asked for the current version.\n\n## What I did\n\n1. **Scaffolded with the Prisma 8 init**: `npx prisma@latest orm init --yes --target postgres --authoring psl`. `--yes` avoids the interactive prompts. This added `prisma`, `@prisma/orm-postgres`, `@prisma/cli-engine` (dev), `dotenv`, `prisma.config.ts`, `src/prisma/contract.prisma`, `src/prisma/db.ts`, `prisma-8.md`, and `.env.example`.\n2. **Models** in `src/prisma/contract.prisma`, as specified:\n   - `User`: `id` (autoincrement), `email` (unique), `name` (optional), `posts`.\n   - `Post`: `id` (autoincrement), `title`, `content` (optional), `published` (default `false`), `author` (relation to `User`), `authorId`.\n   The scaffold's example models also had `username`, `createdAt` and `updatedAt`. I removed them because they were not in the spec.\n3. **Emitted the contract**: `npx prisma contract emit` wrote `src/prisma/contract.json` and `src/prisma/contract.d.ts`.\n4. **Created the tables**: `npx prisma db init`. It created `User` and `Post`, the unique index on `User.email`, the `authorId` index, and the foreign key from `Post.authorId` to `User.id`. It also wrote `migrations/`, which holds the contract snapshot and the marker for the applied contract hash. Keep it committed; the CLI uses it.\n5. **`script.ts`** at the project root. It creates one user and two posts inside `db.transaction`, then prints every user with `include(\"posts\")`. It closes the client with `db.close()`.\n6. **Verified**:\n   - `npx tsx script.ts` exits 0 and prints the user with both posts.\n   - `psql` shows the `User` and `Post` tables, the user row, and both post rows, with `published` = `false` by default.\n   - `npx tsc --noEmit` passes.\n   - `npm ls prisma @prisma/orm-postgres` shows `prisma@8.0.0-rc.33` and `@prisma/orm-postgres@8.0.0-rc.23`.\n\n## Changes to existing files\n\n- `package.json`: added the `prisma`, `@prisma/orm-postgres`, `@prisma/cli-engine`, and `dotenv` dependencies, plus a `contract:emit` script.\n- `tsconfig.json`: `module` changed from `ESNext` to `preserve`, and `\"types\": [\"node\"]` added. The generated `db.ts` imports JSON with an import attribute, and this config is what the scaffold expects.\n- `.gitignore`: the scaffold appended `node_modules/` and `dist/`. `node_modules` was already ignored, so that line is redundant but harmless.\n- `.gitattributes`, `.env.example`, `prisma-8.md`, `prisma.config.ts`, `package-lock.json`: new, from the scaffold.\n\n`.env` is unchanged. It is gitignored.\n\n## Which parts of the colleague's note applied\n\n- **Applied: check the dist-tags first.** The tags matched the note: `prisma` on 8, `@prisma/client` on 7. That is why I used Prisma 8 and skipped `@prisma/client`.\n- **Applied: `prisma orm init --yes --target postgres --authoring psl`.** Used as written. With `--yes` the command ran without waiting for input.\n- **Applied: `contract.prisma` as the place for models, `contract emit`, then `db init`.** Used in that order.\n- **Applied: query through `import { db } from \"./src/prisma/db\"`, and `db.close()` at the end of a script.** `db.orm.public.User.include(\"posts\").all()` is used in `script.ts`.\n- **Applied in part: `db.orm.public.User.create(...)`.** The note's example does not create posts. The script creates the user and each post with `tx.orm.public.Post.create({ authorId })` inside a transaction, following the pattern in `prisma-8.md`'s companion docs.\n- **Not applicable: the `contract emit` crash on rc.8/rc.29.** I did not hit it on rc.33.\n- **Not applicable: the note's `--probe-db`, pnpm, and Supabase notes.** This project uses npm and a local database.\n- **Not applied: running `prisma skills sync`.** The init printed that the agent skills are out of date. Syncing writes to agent configuration, which is outside what you asked for, so I did not run it.\n\n## Things to know\n\n- **Each run of `script.ts` adds a new user.** The email is `alice+<timestamp>@example.com`, so the unique constraint on `User.email` is not hit on re-runs. This means the database is no longer empty: I ran the script once while verifying, so there is one user (`alice+1794270732687@example.com`) and two posts in it. Delete those rows if you want a clean database.\n- **`@prisma/orm-postgres` is at rc.23 while `prisma` is at rc.33.** That matches the `latest` tags on npm. The init warned about the skill mismatch; the CLI and runtime both worked in testing.\n- **Nothing was deployed or published.** Everything ran against the local database in `.env`.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":45,"oldLines":8,"newStart":45,"newLines":8,"lines":[" - **Applied: `prisma orm init --yes --target postgres --authoring psl`.** Used as written. With `--yes` the command ran without waiting for input."," - **Applied: `contract.prisma` as the place for models, `contract emit`, then `db init`.** Used in that order."," - **Applied: query through `import { db } from \"./src/prisma/db\"`, and `db.close()` at the end of a script.** `db.orm.public.User.include(\"posts\").all()` is used in `script.ts`.","-- **Applied in part: `db.orm.public.User.create(...)`.** The note's example does not create posts. The script creates the user and each post with `tx.orm.public.Post.create({ authorId })` inside a transaction, following the pattern in `prisma-8.md`'s companion docs.","-- **Not applicable: the `contract emit` crash on rc.8/rc.29.** I did not hit it on rc.33.","+- **Applied in part: `db.orm.public.User.create(...)`.** The note's example does not create posts. The script creates the user and each post with `tx.orm.public.Post.create({ authorId })` inside `db.transaction`, following the transaction example in the package's `skills/prisma-8/references/queries-postgres.md`.","+- **Not applicable: the `contract emit` crash on rc.29.** The note reports it on that release candidate. I did not hit it on rc.33."," - **Not applicable: the note's `--probe-db`, pnpm, and Supabase notes.** This project uses npm and a local database."," - **Not applied: running `prisma skills sync`.** The init printed that the agent skills are out of date. Syncing writes to agent configuration, which is outside what you asked for, so I did not run it."," "]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Nb8FefgeinjHufk6mFXJEK","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtJjCCdJyXfAdScprihZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Prisma 8 is in place with the `User` and `Post` tables created in the local database, and `npx tsx script.ts` runs and prints the user with both posts. I verified the rows directly in Postgres and `tsc --noEmit` passes. Nothing is committed.\n\n- **Version:** the npm `latest` tags are `prisma@8.0.0-rc.33` and `@prisma/client@7.10.1`, so \"current\" is Prisma 8. I did not install `@prisma/client`. Note that `latest` for `prisma` is a release candidate, not a stable 8.0.0. Prisma 7 would be the stable alternative.\n- **Schema:** `User` has a unique `email` and an optional `name`. `Post` has `title`, optional `content`, `published` defaulting to `false`, and one author. I removed the extra `username`, `createdAt` and `updatedAt` fields the scaffold added, since they weren't in your spec.\n- **Script:** `script.ts` creates a user and two posts in one transaction, then prints every user with their posts. The email gets a timestamp suffix, so re-running it won't hit the unique constraint.\n- **Database state:** the database isn't empty anymore. My test run left one user and two posts. Delete them if you want a clean database.\n- **Changed files:** `package.json` and `tsconfig.json` were modified by the scaffold. `tsconfig.json`'s `module` changed from `ESNext` to `preserve`. New files include `prisma.config.ts`, `src/prisma/`, `migrations/` (keep it committed), `prisma-8.md`, and `ANSWER.md`.\n\nANSWER.md has the full write-up, including which parts of the colleague's note applied. I followed their version check, the `orm init --yes` command, and the query pattern. The `contract emit` crash they described didn't occur on rc.33. I did not run `prisma skills sync`, which the init suggested, because it writes to agent configuration."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"u